                      (    forth6809.asm):00733         
                      (    forth6809.asm):00734         ; ============================================================
                      (    forth6809.asm):00735         ; SECTION 27: FORTH DICTIONARY (ROM base dictionary headers)
                      (    forth6809.asm):00736         ; Every primitive word in the Glossary gets a real header here,
                      (    forth6809.asm):00737         ; chained via LINK, living in BASEDICT ($D83F-$E006, an exact fit
                      (    forth6809.asm):00738         ; for this dictionary's 1992 bytes - was $E000-$E7FF). CFA points
                      (    forth6809.asm):00739         ; directly at each primitive's own code label for every entry -
                      (    forth6809.asm):00740         ; these are all raw code entries, CFA = the label itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):00741         ; including TRUE and FALSE (added in a later pass, chain's newest
                      (    forth6809.asm):00742         ; entries before H_ABORT/H_QUIT below), which originally used the
                      (    forth6809.asm):00743         ; DODOES-trampoline pattern matching interactive CONSTANT, but are
                      (    forth6809.asm):00744         ; now simple LDD/PSHU/RTS subroutines like everything else here -
                      (    forth6809.asm):00745         ; see TRUEBODY/FALSEBODY, section 26, for the current code and why
                      (    forth6809.asm):00746         ; they no longer need indirection.
                      (    forth6809.asm):00747         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):00748         ; DOES> is included (H_DOESGT) - added in a follow-up pass after
                      (    forth6809.asm):00749         ; the original 214-entry generation flagged it as missing, then
                      (    forth6809.asm):00750         ; moved again so it sits immediately after CREATE in the chain
                      (    forth6809.asm):00751         ; (H_CREATE -> H_DOESGT -> H_VARIABLE) rather than at the chain's
                      (    forth6809.asm):00752         ; newest end, since the two words are tightly coupled and read
                      (    forth6809.asm):00753         ; better adjacent. SETDOES (the runtime it compiles a call to)
                      (    forth6809.asm):00754         ; lives beside DODOES/DOESRT0; DOESGT is DOES>'s code label,
                      (    forth6809.asm):00755         ; since a literal ">" is not valid in a 6809 assembler label.
                      (    forth6809.asm):00756         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):00757         ; H_ABORT and H_QUIT (formerly ABORTHDR/QUITHDR, renamed to match
                      (    forth6809.asm):00758         ; this file's H_ naming convention) are hand-built, not produced
                      (    forth6809.asm):00759         ; by the same generation pass as the other 217 entries - see the
