                      (    forth6809.asm):06148                    ; ALGORITHM REPLACED (caught by MAME testing after the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06149                    ; argument-order fix above): the entire body below used
                      (    forth6809.asm):06150                    ; to decode backslash escape sequences (\n, \t, \\, \") -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06151                    ; a plausible-looking but entirely wrong reading of what
                      (    forth6809.asm):06152                    ; ANS UNESCAPE does. Confirmed against the actual spec and
                      (    forth6809.asm):06153                    ; its canonical reference implementation (forth-standard.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06154                    ; org/standard/string/UNESCAPE and complang.tuwien.ac.at's
                      (    forth6809.asm):06155                    ; ANS Forth reference text): UNESCAPE has nothing to do
                      (    forth6809.asm):06156                    ; with backslash sequences at all - it replaces every '%'
                      (    forth6809.asm):06157                    ; character with two '%' characters, and nothing else, so
                      (    forth6809.asm):06158                    ; that a literal '%' in text survives an eventual
                      (    forth6809.asm):06159                    ; SUBSTITUTE pass unchanged ("If you pass a string through
                      (    forth6809.asm):06160                    ; UNESCAPE and then SUBSTITUTE, you get the original
                      (    forth6809.asm):06161                    ; string"). Every character that ISN'T '%' passes straight
                      (    forth6809.asm):06162                    ; through, one-for-one. Confirmed via MAME: doubling a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06163                    ; single '%' wasn't happening at all, and the returned
                      (    forth6809.asm):06164                    ; count didn't grow to reflect the added characters -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06165                    ; both are direct, expected consequences of this being the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06166                    ; wrong algorithm entirely, not a smaller bug within it.
