                      (    forth6809.asm):06477                                  ; before the branch that depends on it. The
                      (    forth6809.asm):06478                                  ; four existing internal callers (DOT/DOTR/
                      (    forth6809.asm):06479                                  ; DDOT/DDOTR, i.e. . / .R / D. / D.R) were
                      (    forth6809.asm):06480                                  ; accidentally unaffected - each happens to
                      (    forth6809.asm):06481                                  ; run "LDD SAVEN" (a flag-setting load of the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06482                                  ; true signed value) immediately before PSHU
                      (    forth6809.asm):06483                                  ; D/JSR SIGN, and PSHU doesn't disturb flags -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06484                                  ; but this was fragile, caller-side luck, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):06485                                  ; SIGN being correct on its own. Confirmed via
