                      (    forth6809.asm):06816         ; ENVIRONMENT? - dispatcher complete; table has entries derived
                      (    forth6809.asm):06817         ; without fabricating unfixed capacities. /HOLD and /PAD were both
                      (    forth6809.asm):06818         ; added this session, answering HOLDMINSIZE and PADMINSIZE
                      (    forth6809.asm):06819         ; respectively (see each entry itself, below, for why each uses its
                      (    forth6809.asm):06820         ; own, conceptually correct constant rather than the numerically-
                      (    forth6809.asm):06821         ; equal PADOFFSET).
                      (    forth6809.asm):06822         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06823         ; WORDLISTS (16.3.2, Search-Order word set) is deliberately absent
                      (    forth6809.asm):06824         ; from ENVTABLE, not an oversight - this system doesn't implement
                      (    forth6809.asm):06825         ; the Search-Order word set, so WORDLISTS is genuinely an unknown
                      (    forth6809.asm):06826         ; attribute here. Per ENVIRONMENT?'s own spec (6.1.1345): "If the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06827         ; system treats the attribute as unknown, the returned flag is
                      (    forth6809.asm):06828         ; false" - falling through to ENVNOTFOUND already produces exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):06829         ; that, correctly and completely, with no dispatcher work needed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06830         ; Confirmed via MAME testing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06831         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06832         ; MAX-D/MAX-UD were resolved this session via a genuine dispatcher
                      (    forth6809.asm):06833         ; extension, not just a table entry - both are double-cell values
                      (    forth6809.asm):06834         ; per their own ANS data type, which the original single-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):06835         ; ENVFOUND (pushing exactly one value before TRUE) couldn't
                      (    forth6809.asm):06836         ; represent. Added a second table (ENVTABLE2) and matching loop
                      (    forth6809.asm):06837         ; (ENV2START/ENV2LOOP/ENV2FOUND, below) specifically for double-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):06838         ; entries, rather than reworking the single-cell path to handle both
                      (    forth6809.asm):06839         ; shapes - see those labels for the full design.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06840         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):06841         ; FLOORED was the third, separate open item flagged previously -
                      (    forth6809.asm):06842         ; investigated this session by tracing DIVCOMMON (shared by /, MOD,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06843         ; /MOD) against this system's own SM/REM and FM/MOD. Confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):06844         ; DIVCOMMON matches SM/REM's convention exactly (remainder sign
                      (    forth6809.asm):06845         ; restored from the dividend's own original sign, not the quotient's)
                      (    forth6809.asm):06846         ; - this system's primary division words use symmetric division, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):06847         ; floored. FLOORED now answers 0 (false) - see the entry itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06848         ; below, for the full trace.
FD08 3706             (    forth6809.asm):06849         ENVQUERY: PULU D
